Cg a60.375000,61.000000,788
{\rtf1\ansi \deff0
{\fonttbl
{\f0\fnil Arial;}
{\f1\fnil Symbol;}
{\f2\fnil CG Times;}
}
{\plain {\b \ulnone \f0 \i0 Project }{\b 
\ulnone \f0 \i0 1.2}{\f0 \b0 \i0   (a) Create
 a new Mathcad document and d}{\f0 \i0 \b0 
\b0 efine an analog pulse train, using a
 function definition and Mathcad's ability
 to sum functions, and then sample it. Plot
 both the analog and digital signals. (b)
 Now }{\f0 \b0 \i0 \f0 choose each pulse
 amplitude to be randomly +/- 1; such an
 amplitude sequence represents a }{\f0 \b0 
\i0 \b \i0 \f0 binary sequence}{\f0 \b0 
\i0 \f0 , a model for a communication message.
 (c) Add a sequence of normal noise, of 
zero mean and variance var, to the digital
 sequence. Implement a simple "receiver"
 to extract an estimate of the binary sequence
 from the "signal plus noise sequence". 
Count the errors and study their number 
versus the "signal to noise ratio" 1/var.}}
}
.TXT 19 2 3 0
Cg a49.250000,73.000000,72
{\rtf1\ansi \deff0
{\fonttbl
{\f0\fnil Arial;}
{\f1\fnil Symbol;}
{\f2\fnil CG Times;}
}
{\plain {We can use a function definition
 to implement an analog  pulse, p(t).}}
}
